@Kranael the `page.request` is using the proxy settings that you set up in config. If you're using just the `request` fixture, than it doesn't use the `proxy` settings in the config.

Which one do you use?

You can always try creating your own `APIRequestContext` with proper proxy settings and see if it works: https://playwright.dev/docs/next/api/class-apirequest#api-request-new-context-option-proxy

@aslushnikov thank you very much for confirmation and the information.

I have a question now -> Is there a reason to let the request fixture not use global config?

So now i know why it works when we set up a context but not with the fixture. I know i can modify or even create a new fixture but i thought that the config is always used from your default fixtures baked in the framework. Why not the "request" fixture?

I also have this issue in 1.32, it was working fine in 1.31. I'm making requests to localhost via the `request` fixture and had localhost listed in `config.use.proxy.bypass`, but now the requests are sent to the proxy.

Even explicitly creating a request context like this:
```
const requestContext = await request.newContext({
      baseURL: "http://localhost:8080",
      proxy: { server: "proxy.example.com", bypass: "localhost" },
    });
```
or like this
```
const requestContext = await request.newContext({
      baseURL: "http://localhost:8080",
      proxy: { server: "proxy.example.com", bypass: "localhost:8080" },
    });
```
the requests still appear to go over the proxy.

